<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0">
  <head><title>Rider platform: end-to-end workflow (passenger, driver, money)</title></head>
  <body>
    <outline text="Rider platform workflow">
      <outline text="Passenger journey">
        <outline text="P1. Enable current location [partly built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="The app asks for location permission and reads the phone's GPS. The backend checks the point is inside a service area."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="GET /zones/check?lat={lat}&amp;lng={lng}"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="Rides can only start inside an active service zone (Gulshan &amp; Banani, Dhanmondi, Uttara, Mirpur, Motijheel in the demo data)."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Note">
            <outline text="The zone check is built. Reading GPS is a mobile-app job (app not built)."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="P2. Choose pickup and destination [partly built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="Pickup defaults to the current location. The passenger picks or types the destination. A place copied from Google Maps (e.g. '23.7806, 90.4074') is turned into latitude and longitude by the app."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="No call yet: the points are sent with the quote in P3."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="Each point is latitude, longitude and an optional name (up to 200 characters)."/>
            <outline text="The pickup must be inside a service zone; the destination may be outside it."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Note">
            <outline text="The API takes coordinates and names. Pasting 'lat, lng' is supported in the admin 'Book a ride' drawer today. Reading a full Google Maps share link (https://maps.app.goo.gl/...) and place search need the app plus a geocoding provider (Google Places or Barikoi), not built."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="P3. Search: see the fare and the drivers nearby [partly built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="The passenger picks a vehicle type (Bike, Car, CNG). The system calculates the route distance and time, prices the ride from the live fare rule (including any surge) and counts the available drivers nearby."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="POST /quotes  { category_id, pickup: {lat, lng, label}, destination: {lat, lng, label} }"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Returns">
            <outline text="quote id"/>
            <outline text="estimated fare and its breakdown"/>
            <outline text="surge multiplier"/>
            <outline text="number of available drivers nearby"/>
            <outline text="quote expiry time"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="The fare is frozen in the quote: the passenger pays what they were shown (plus waiting time or a changed route)."/>
            <outline text="Distance and time come from Google Routes when configured, otherwise from an estimate."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Note">
            <outline text="Built: fare, surge and the COUNT of nearby drivers. Not built: showing each nearby driver on the passenger's map (needs a privacy-safe 'nearby drivers' endpoint that returns approximate positions only)."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="P4. Request the ride [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="The passenger confirms the quote, chooses cash and can add a pickup note or a promo code. The request goes to dispatch."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="POST /rides  { quote_id, payment_method: 'cash', pickup_note }   then optionally  POST /rides/{id}/promo  { code }"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="ONE active request per passenger: a second request is refused until the first is cancelled, completed or expired."/>
            <outline text="Only cash is enabled (setting payments.enabled_methods). Digital payments are not built."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="P5. Driver matching [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="Dispatch offers the ride to the NEAREST free driver with the right vehicle type. That driver has 15 seconds to accept. If they decline or don't answer, the next nearest driver gets the offer. The search widens from 1.5 km to 3 km to 5 km. With nobody after 3 minutes the request closes as 'no driver found'."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="GET /rides/{id}  (passenger watches the status: searching → matched)"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="A ride is offered to one driver at a time; a driver gets one offer at a time."/>
            <outline text="Only approved, online drivers with a fresh location and an active vehicle of that type are offered rides."/>
            <outline text="Staff can re-dispatch, assign a specific driver or cancel from the admin panel (Ride requests)."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Who picks whom">
            <outline text="Driver picks passenger: Built: the driver sees the offer (pickup, destination, fare, distance) and accepts or declines it (see D4)."/>
            <outline text="Passenger picks driver: Not built. Today the system picks the nearest driver automatically, which is faster and fairer. If you want passengers to choose, the change is: show 3–5 nearby drivers with name, rating, vehicle and ETA after the quote, the passenger taps one, and that driver alone gets the offer (if they decline or time out, the passenger chooses again). The one-active-request and one-offer-per-driver locks stay the same."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="P6. Driver assigned: track the driver [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="The passenger sees the driver's name, rating, vehicle and plate, and follows the driver's progress: on the way → arrived."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="GET /rides/{id}   (realtime channel 'ride:{id}' also announces each status change)"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="If the pickup PIN feature flag is on, the passenger reads a 4-digit PIN to the driver at pickup (GET /rides/{id}/pin)."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="P7. Cancel (the standard way) [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="Before the ride starts the passenger can cancel. The app first shows whether a fee applies, then cancels with a reason."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="GET /rides/{id}/cancel-preview   then   POST /rides/{id}/cancel  { reason }"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="Free while searching, and within 2 minutes of a driver being assigned."/>
            <outline text="Later, a cancellation fee applies (Bike 30, Car 50, CNG 40 in the demo fare rules). It is added to the passenger's next ride; the driver receives it minus the platform commission."/>
            <outline text="A ride that has started cannot be cancelled by the passenger."/>
            <outline text="After cancelling, the passenger is free to request again."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="P8. Ride in progress and completed [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="The driver starts the trip at pickup and completes it at the destination. The final fare is calculated from the frozen fare rule and the recorded route, time and waiting."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="GET /rides/{id}   then   GET /trips/{id}/receipt"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="SOS is available throughout the ride: POST /trips/{id}/sos alerts the safety team at once (with evidence upload)."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="P9. Pay the driver [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="The passenger pays the final fare in cash to the driver (fare minus any promo discount, plus any cancellation fee owed from earlier)."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="GET /trips/{id}/receipt  (shows the amount to pay)"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="The driver confirms the cash in their app (D7). Unconfirmed cash is flagged to finance after 24 hours."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Note">
            <outline text="bKash / Nagad / card payment is not built (needs merchant accounts); see docs/integrations/digital-payments.md."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="P10. Rate and review the driver [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="The passenger gives 1–5 stars and an optional comment. The driver can rate the passenger the same way."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="POST /trips/{id}/rate  { score: 1-5, comment }"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="Once per trip, within 7 days of completion (setting ratings.window_days)."/>
            <outline text="Ratings feed the driver's average rating. Staff can hide abusive comments (Ratings page, with a reason)."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="P11. Help after the ride [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="Lost item, overcharge or complaint: the passenger opens a support ticket. Staff can refund (approved by finance)."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="POST /support/tickets  { tripId, category, subject, body }"/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="Driver journey">
        <outline text="D1. Sign up and onboard [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="The driver creates an account, fills in details, adds a vehicle and uploads documents (NID, driving licence, profile photo, registration, fitness, tax token, insurance; route permit for CNG), then submits the application."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="POST /onboarding/driver → PATCH /driver/details → POST /driver/vehicles → POST /driver/documents/upload-url + POST /driver/documents/{id}/complete → POST /driver/application/submit"/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="D2. Approval by the organisation [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="Operations reviews each document (approve or reject with a reason), verifies the vehicle and approves the driver. Staff can also create the driver and upload documents for them."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Where in the admin panel">
            <outline text="Admin panel → Drivers → Review application; Documents queue"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="Expired documents suspend the driver automatically until renewed."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="D3. Go online [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="The driver goes online. The app sends the driver's location every few seconds so dispatch knows who is nearby."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="POST /driver/availability  { online: true, lat, lng }   then   POST /driver/location  (batched points)"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="A driver whose location stops updating for 2 minutes is taken offline automatically."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="D4. Pick a passenger (accept an offer) [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="The driver gets an offer showing the pickup, destination, fare and pickup distance, and has 15 seconds to accept or decline."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="GET /driver/offers/current   then   POST /driver/offers/{id}/accept   or   POST /driver/offers/{id}/reject"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="ONE pending offer and ONE active trip per driver: no new offers until the current trip ends or is cancelled."/>
            <outline text="If several drivers race to accept, exactly one wins; the others get 'offer no longer available'."/>
            <outline text="Declines and timeouts count towards the driver's acceptance rate."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="D5. Drive to the pickup and start [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="On the way → arrived (the system checks the driver is near the pickup) → start the trip (entering the passenger's PIN when that feature is on)."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="POST /driver/trips/{id}/arriving → POST /driver/trips/{id}/arrived → POST /driver/trips/{id}/start  { pin }"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="Waiting at pickup beyond the free minutes (3 in the demo rules) is charged per minute."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="D6. Cancel (the standard way) [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="Before the trip starts the driver can cancel with a reason (e.g. passenger not reachable). The request closes and the passenger can request again."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="POST /driver/trips/{id}/cancel  { reason }"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="Cancellations count towards the driver's cancellation rate. Repeated late cancellations can lead to suspension by staff."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="D7. Complete the ride and collect cash [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="At the destination the driver completes the trip. The app shows the amount to collect; the driver takes the cash and confirms it."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="POST /driver/trips/{id}/complete   then   POST /driver/trips/{id}/cash-collected"/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="D8. See earnings and wallet [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="The driver sees each trip's earning (fare minus platform commission) and their wallet: negative means they owe the organisation (cash they kept that includes the platform's share); positive means the organisation owes them."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="GET /driver/earnings   and   GET /driver/wallet"/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="D9. Pay the organisation (cash dues) [built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="Because passengers pay cash to the driver, the driver holds the platform's commission. The driver deposits it by bKash, Nagad, bank or at the office; finance records the deposit and it clears the dues."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Where in the admin panel">
            <outline text="Admin panel → Payments → Driver dues → Record deposit"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="Finance reconciles cash and deposits; differences raise an alert."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="D10. Get paid by the organisation (payouts) [partly built]">
          <outline text="What happens">
            <outline text="When a driver's wallet is positive (promo discounts the platform covered, incentives, cancellation fees), finance creates a weekly payout batch, a second finance person approves it, and the money is sent to the driver's verified bKash / Nagad / bank account and marked paid."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="API call">
            <outline text="Driver: PUT /driver/payout-account  { method, holder, ref }"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Where in the admin panel">
            <outline text="Admin panel → Payouts"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Rules">
            <outline text="Only balances of at least 500 are paid (setting payouts.minimum_amount)."/>
            <outline text="The person who creates a batch cannot approve it (maker–checker)."/>
            <outline text="Sending the money is manual today (bKash merchant portal or bank upload); automatic payout needs a provider API, see docs/integrations/payout-provider.md."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="Money and profit">
        <outline text="How cash moves">
          <outline text="Passenger pays the full fare in cash to the driver"/>
          <outline text="Driver deposits the organisation's share (bKash, Nagad, bank or office)"/>
          <outline text="Organisation pays the driver what it owes (promo discounts, incentives, cancellation fees) in the weekly payout"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Fare">
          <outline text="fare = max(minimum fare, base + per_km × km + per_minute × minutes + waiting) × surge  + booking fee"/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Who gets what">
          <outline text="driver">
            <outline text="fare − platform commission (commission is a percentage of the fare, set per fare rule)"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="organisation">
            <outline text="platform commission + booking fee + commission share of cancellation fees"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="organisation costs">
            <outline text="promo discounts (the platform funds them), driver incentives, approved refunds"/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Worked examples">
          <outline text="Bike, 6 km, 18 minutes, cash, no promo">
            <outline text="fare: 25 + 6×12 + 18×1 = 115"/>
            <outline text="passenger pays driver: 115"/>
            <outline text="driver earning: 115 − 15% (17.25) = 97.75"/>
            <outline text="organisation earns: 17.25"/>
            <outline text="settlement: The driver holds 115 but earned 97.75, so the driver wallet shows −17.25: the driver deposits 17.25 to the organisation (D9)."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Same ride with promo WELCOME50 (platform pays the 50)">
            <outline text="fare: 115"/>
            <outline text="passenger pays driver: 65"/>
            <outline text="driver earning: 97.75"/>
            <outline text="organisation earns: 17.25 commission − 50 promo = −32.75 (a marketing cost)"/>
            <outline text="settlement: The driver holds 65 but earned 97.75, so the wallet shows +32.75: the organisation pays the driver 32.75 in the next payout (D10)."/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Car, 8 km, 25 minutes, cash">
            <outline text="fare: 60 + 8×30 + 25×3 = 375, plus booking fee 10 = 385"/>
            <outline text="passenger pays driver: 385"/>
            <outline text="driver earning: 375 − 20% (75) = 300"/>
            <outline text="organisation earns: 75 commission + 10 booking fee = 85"/>
            <outline text="settlement: Driver wallet −85: deposited to the organisation."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Organisation profit">
          <outline text="Revenue">
            <outline text="Commission on every completed ride"/>
            <outline text="Booking fee (car and CNG)"/>
            <outline text="Commission share of passenger cancellation fees"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Minus">
            <outline text="Promotions the platform funds"/>
            <outline text="Driver incentives (approved adjustments)"/>
            <outline text="Refunds"/>
            <outline text="Running costs outside this system (maps, SMS, hosting, staff)"/>
          </outline>
          <outline text="Where to see it">
            <outline text="Admin panel → Dashboard (gross bookings, platform revenue, contribution per ride), Analytics → Economics and Finance, Ledger (platform accounts)."/>
          </outline>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Controls">
          <outline text="Fares are frozen at quote time."/>
          <outline text="Refunds and adjustments need a second approver from 5,000 up (setting finance.dual_approval_threshold)."/>
          <outline text="The ledger is checked every night; any imbalance raises an alert."/>
          <outline text="Every staff action needs a reason and is written to the audit log."/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="One-at-a-time rules">
        <outline text="passenger">
          <outline text="One active request at a time. To book another ride, cancel the current one (standard cancel, fee rules apply) or wait until it completes or expires."/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="driver">
          <outline text="One pending offer and one active trip at a time. A new offer comes only after the current trip is completed or cancelled."/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="race safety">
          <outline text="If many drivers accept the same ride at once, exactly one gets it (tested with 50 drivers at once)."/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
      <outline text="Not built yet">
        <outline text="Passenger and driver mobile apps">
          <outline text="The API they need is built; see docs/spec/05-api.md."/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Passenger chooses a specific driver">
          <outline text="Today: automatic nearest-driver dispatch, or staff assign a driver. Design for passenger choice is in P5."/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Nearby drivers drawn on the passenger's map">
          <outline text="Today: the quote returns the count of nearby drivers."/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Google Maps share links and place search">
          <outline text="Needs the app and a geocoding provider (Google Places or Barikoi)."/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="bKash / Nagad / card payment by the passenger">
          <outline text="Needs merchant accounts; see docs/integrations/digital-payments.md."/>
        </outline>
        <outline text="Automatic payouts to drivers">
          <outline text="Today finance sends payouts by hand and marks them paid; see docs/integrations/payout-provider.md."/>
        </outline>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  </body>
</opml>
